mode: "100644"
text: "# The SCOUT framework — recon for the gap, not a copy\n\nMost accounts either ignore competitors or mimic them — both lose. SCOUT is **reconnaissance**: read\nthe public landscape to find the **white space you can own**, then differentiate. Public data only; no\nscraping, impersonation, or copying.\n\n## S — Select the field\n- Roster **direct + aspirational + adjacent** competitors (~5–8). Include the incumbent behaviour or\n  \"do nothing\" you're displacing.\n- **Match by industry, audience, and format** — don't compare unlike things.\n\n## C — Capture public signals\n- For each: **positioning/message, content pillars, formats & mix, posting cadence, hooks & tone,\n  visual style, CTAs**, and **paid** creative (Meta Ad Library / TikTok Creative Center).\n- **Public only.** Capture what any user can see; note where you're inferring vs observing.\n\n## O — Observe what works\n- Read **engagement RATE, share of voice, and growth trend** — *not* follower counts. When a post\n  spikes, ask **why** (giveaway? influencer share? trend? format?).\n- **Benchmark relative** to the direct set over time (platform averages mislead — TikTok ~3.7% vs\n  Facebook ~0.15%). Add **AI/LLM visibility** (are they cited by ChatGPT/Gemini/Claude?).\n\n## U — Uncover the white space\n- Map the **gap**: topics that earn engagement nobody in the set covers; **formats** they ignore;\n  **audiences** underserved; a **POV** unclaimed; a **funnel stage** (strong awareness, weak\n  conversion) left open; a **service/voice** gap (rivals formal → you human).\n- The win is **different, not louder.**\n\n## T — Translate to your strategy\n- Convert the gap into **your pillars, positioning, cadence, and format mix** — staying in *your*\n  brand voice (don't adopt theirs). **Test a gap with clear KPIs** before scaling.\n- Feed **social-strategy** and **content-pillars**; re-run the loop **monthly/quarterly**.\n\n## The competitor-analysis brief a request should fill\n```\nFIELD: 5–8 competitors (direct / aspirational / adjacent), matched by industry+audience+format\nSIGNALS: positioning, pillars, formats, cadence, hooks, tone, visuals, CTAs, paid (public only)\nWORKS: engagement rate + SOV + growth trend (not followers); why the spikes; AI/LLM visibility\nWHITE SPACE: the topic/format/audience/POV/funnel/service gap you can own\nTRANSLATE: into your pillars/positioning/cadence (your voice); test with KPIs -> social-strategy\n```\n\n> Not SCOUT's job: why a *single post* worked → **viral-reverse-engineering**; *your* audience →\n> **audience-research**; timely cultural moments → **trend-jacking**; *your* plan → **social-strategy**.\n"
